WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:42.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.106 --> 00:50.071
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
00:50.155 --> 00:51.573
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND INCIDENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

4
00:51.656 --> 00:53.074
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED UNDER GUIDELINES

5
00:57.036 --> 00:58.329
Can you trust me?

6
01:00.623 --> 01:03.585
No matter what I do or say?

7
01:06.004 --> 01:08.423
You don't have to answer me right now.

8
01:09.340 --> 01:10.175
But…

9
01:13.136 --> 01:14.095
for now…

10
01:16.014 --> 01:17.223
I just want you to trust me.

11
01:24.147 --> 01:24.981
Lee Ga-kyung.

12
01:25.982 --> 01:26.816
Yes?

13
01:30.695 --> 01:31.529
I mean…

14
01:32.155 --> 01:33.615
I wasn't answering you.

15
01:34.490 --> 01:35.450
Lee Ga-kyung suits you…

16
01:37.785 --> 01:39.829
much better than Keum Seo-hee.

17
01:44.209 --> 01:46.127
Lee Ga-kyung.

18
01:50.340 --> 01:52.008
May I call you that?

19
01:55.511 --> 01:57.263
I do want an answer to that now.

20
02:11.569 --> 02:12.403
Yes…

21
02:15.657 --> 02:18.785
Interpreter Kim Tae-ung.

22
02:41.683 --> 02:45.603
The inspector general invited you to dinner at his residence?

23
02:46.479 --> 02:47.313
That's right.

24
02:48.773 --> 02:49.607
So-ran.

25
02:50.316 --> 02:53.152
I really don't think it's a good idea to go.

26
02:53.236 --> 02:56.406
There's no way he'd invite us over just for a pleasant evening.

27
02:57.699 --> 02:58.741
Exactly.

28
02:59.325 --> 03:01.661
The inspector general seemed smarter than that.

29
03:01.744 --> 03:04.038
Does he think you'll come running just because he asked?

30
03:04.122 --> 03:06.124
We weren't born yesterday.

31
03:10.878 --> 03:12.297
Are you thinking of going?

32
03:12.964 --> 03:13.798
You're not, right?

33
03:16.259 --> 03:17.552
You can't.

34
03:17.635 --> 03:19.137
This has to be a trap.

35
03:19.220 --> 03:23.016
He already knows the Gugukdan set off the bomb at the banquet.

36
03:23.099 --> 03:25.435
Wouldn't it look more suspicious if we didn't go?

37
03:26.728 --> 03:27.603
So-ran.

38
03:28.396 --> 03:31.566
We can't even get a knife past security at the residence.

39
03:31.649 --> 03:34.027
I'll come up with some kind of excuse.

40
03:34.110 --> 03:35.862
Let's not take any chances this time.

41
03:35.945 --> 03:37.530
Let's wait for the right time--

42
03:37.613 --> 03:39.782
There may never be a right time.

43
03:40.700 --> 03:42.744
Sato's already closing in on us.

44
03:42.827 --> 03:45.246
We'll have to face it sooner or later,

45
03:45.330 --> 03:47.332
and we're really running out of time.

46
03:50.251 --> 03:52.795
Still, it's too dangerous without any weapons.

47
03:52.879 --> 03:54.839
Then I'll break a glass and use that.

48
03:55.465 --> 03:57.925
So-ran, we'll be in his house.

49
03:58.009 --> 03:59.761
I can't risk losing you there.

50
04:19.280 --> 04:20.239
In that case,

51
04:21.324 --> 04:22.158
you should go.

52
04:24.911 --> 04:26.079
But…

53
04:27.080 --> 04:28.998
I have an idea.

54
04:32.085 --> 04:34.295
Send a bomb to the residence through the pneumatic tube?

55
04:34.379 --> 04:35.338
Yes.

56
04:35.963 --> 04:38.966
Do you all remember this pneumatic tube thing?

57
04:41.177 --> 04:44.972
The pneumatic tube system connects the Government-General and Keijo Post Office.

58
04:45.056 --> 04:48.851
It also links the Government-General with both the governor-general's residence

59
04:48.935 --> 04:51.145
and the inspector general's residence.

60
04:51.229 --> 04:54.148
The pneumatic tube carriers, canisters that travel through the tubes,

61
04:54.232 --> 04:58.319
are about this big, more than big enough to fit a bomb.

62
04:58.403 --> 05:00.613
And we've got two bombs

63
05:00.696 --> 05:02.698
right here, in the ladies' room.

64
05:02.782 --> 05:05.243
It's right next to the pneumatic tube room.

65
05:05.827 --> 05:08.329
The carriers take just two and a half minutes

66
05:08.413 --> 05:10.456
to reach the residences from the Government-General.

67
05:10.540 --> 05:13.167
I've seen the technical documents and interpreted for them.

68
05:13.251 --> 05:15.128
Trust me, it takes two and a half minutes.

69
05:16.003 --> 05:17.380
Two and a half minutes.

70
05:17.463 --> 05:20.466
So we could get a bomb into both residences

71
05:20.550 --> 05:23.678
in just two and a half minutes, past all that security?

72
05:23.761 --> 05:25.721
The bombs are already in the Government-General.

73
05:25.805 --> 05:27.849
The governor-general hasn't left his residence.

74
05:27.932 --> 05:31.477
This is our chance to take out both men in one strike.

75
05:31.561 --> 05:33.146
But you'll be in there too.

76
05:34.564 --> 05:35.648
Can you escape in time?

77
05:35.731 --> 05:38.151
I'll keep Sato in the study where the pneumatic tube is,

78
05:38.234 --> 05:39.235
then slip away.

79
05:39.318 --> 05:41.070
We have no more time to waste.

80
05:41.154 --> 05:43.156
We need to do whatever we can.

81
05:43.906 --> 05:44.907
Ms. Ga-kyung.

82
05:44.991 --> 05:45.950
I mean,

83
05:46.033 --> 05:47.577
-Ms. Seo-hee. -Yes.

84
05:47.660 --> 05:50.079
Anything else we should know about the pneumatic tube system?

85
05:51.080 --> 05:53.916
Before sending a carrier, the staff call the residence first

86
05:54.000 --> 05:55.334
to let them know it's on its way.

87
05:55.418 --> 05:56.919
A pneumatic tube carrier is coming

88
05:57.003 --> 05:58.838
from the inspector general to the governor-general,

89
05:58.921 --> 05:59.797
so please stand by.

90
06:03.468 --> 06:05.887
Two and a half minutes later, it arrives at the residence.

91
06:13.186 --> 06:16.481
The residence staff hand it over to the governor-general or inspector general.

92
06:18.274 --> 06:21.235
Factoring in the time it'll take to reach the recipient,

93
06:21.319 --> 06:23.821
we'd need a bomb with a four-minute timer.

94
06:27.241 --> 06:28.075
Yes?

95
06:29.827 --> 06:32.788
We need to send the carriers to both residences almost at the same time.

96
06:36.709 --> 06:40.254
There's a chance that one of them could open the carrier

97
06:41.005 --> 06:42.465
before the four minutes are up.

98
06:49.013 --> 06:52.850
So we'll have to modify the bombs to explode the moment

99
06:53.559 --> 06:54.977
the carriers are opened.

100
06:59.065 --> 07:01.400
Is there any way I could get into the Government-General?

101
07:03.069 --> 07:05.238
Security must be extremely tight right now.

102
07:07.490 --> 07:10.952
Normally, the customer is supposed to pick it up on the first floor.

103
07:11.035 --> 07:13.204
But "Toilet" makes me bring it inside.

104
07:13.287 --> 07:14.163
And that's every day.

105
07:15.581 --> 07:16.415
There's a way.

106
07:19.293 --> 07:22.255
I know someone who really loves naengmyeon.

107
07:24.757 --> 07:31.222
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

108
07:31.305 --> 07:33.599
EPISODE 12

109
07:46.487 --> 07:48.155
Please make sure Sato Hideo,

110
07:48.239 --> 07:49.949
the bastard who killed Songjeon,

111
07:50.032 --> 07:52.159
is in the study with the inspector general.

112
07:52.785 --> 07:56.122
Our targets are the governor-general and inspector general.

113
07:56.205 --> 07:58.040
Let's focus on our targets for now

114
07:58.124 --> 07:59.500
and leave the rest to fate.

115
08:01.586 --> 08:02.461
Seo-hee.

116
08:03.254 --> 08:05.047
You and Se-hwan

117
08:05.673 --> 08:08.342
need to leave the Government-General the moment you send the bombs.

118
08:09.218 --> 08:10.970
Lay low somewhere safe for a while.

119
08:11.804 --> 08:13.973
We'll move again when things settle down.

120
08:15.850 --> 08:18.728
I guess tomorrow will be my last day

121
08:19.478 --> 08:21.063
working at the Government-General.

122
08:24.150 --> 08:26.902
He can't go to the residence today.

123
08:26.986 --> 08:29.405
But he can't stay here either.

124
08:30.906 --> 08:31.907
Then…

125
08:32.575 --> 08:36.579
this might be the last time I ever see him.

126
08:41.834 --> 08:43.252
Do you have a headache?

127
08:45.254 --> 08:46.130
No.

128
08:47.757 --> 08:48.966
Your face says

129
08:49.634 --> 08:51.344
you're having a rough day.

130
09:01.103 --> 09:01.937
I feel like…

131
09:03.814 --> 09:05.983
English is starting to stress me out today.

132
09:07.443 --> 09:08.277
So,

133
09:09.153 --> 09:10.279
I'm going to head out first.

134
09:10.363 --> 09:11.238
What?

135
09:11.947 --> 09:12.907
You scared me.

136
09:13.407 --> 09:14.241
What is it?

137
09:16.327 --> 09:17.328
Well…

138
09:18.037 --> 09:19.538
Are you leaving for the day?

139
09:20.122 --> 09:23.459
Are you heading to the residence, then?

140
09:23.542 --> 09:26.003
No, I'm on my way to see Mr. Kim.

141
09:27.505 --> 09:30.007
Why are you meeting him?

142
09:30.091 --> 09:31.384
What do you mean, why?

143
09:31.467 --> 09:33.094
I need to talk to him about Gyodang-ri.

144
09:35.388 --> 09:39.225
I was going to arrange a meeting with him to discuss what happened yesterday.

145
09:39.308 --> 09:40.351
When I got home,

146
09:40.434 --> 09:42.436
he'd already invited me to dinner today.

147
09:45.481 --> 09:48.234
I guess you'll be getting home late, then.

148
09:48.818 --> 09:49.694
What a relief.

149
09:51.070 --> 09:52.613
Sorry? What was that?

150
09:53.447 --> 09:54.824
It's nothing.

151
09:57.326 --> 10:00.705
I know we've got a lot of work to do. Sorry for taking off early.

152
10:02.540 --> 10:04.375
You should call it a day early.

153
10:04.458 --> 10:06.711
We can finish the rest together tomorrow.

154
10:10.381 --> 10:12.383
All right, I'm off.

155
10:14.593 --> 10:15.469
Kim Tae-ung!

156
10:16.345 --> 10:17.388
What?

157
10:20.224 --> 10:21.976
Mr. Kim.

158
10:25.604 --> 10:28.691
You're just going to call me by my name now?

159
10:29.692 --> 10:31.152
Then I'll call you by your name too.

160
10:31.861 --> 10:33.738
Lee Ga-kyung.

161
10:39.243 --> 10:40.077
What is it?

162
10:41.454 --> 10:43.414
Do you have something to say to me?

163
10:50.087 --> 10:51.005
Take care.

164
10:52.006 --> 10:54.175
I'll see you when you get back.

165
10:56.218 --> 10:57.094
Thanks.

166
10:58.012 --> 10:59.722
I'll see you tomorrow, then.

167
11:02.057 --> 11:04.435
Oh, right.

168
11:04.518 --> 11:07.605
I've got a little sister. Her name is Hanako.

169
11:08.439 --> 11:09.690
Your little sister?

170
11:09.774 --> 11:13.611
Yes, you met her briefly at Gyeongseong Station.

171
11:14.528 --> 11:17.323
It was the day someone stole my wallet.

172
11:19.074 --> 11:20.367
Hey, hold on.

173
11:23.287 --> 11:24.997
You mean that girl from…

174
11:25.790 --> 11:26.624
Yes.

175
11:27.291 --> 11:29.543
She's my Joseon mother's biological daughter.

176
11:30.586 --> 11:31.587
Hanako…

177
11:34.507 --> 11:36.050
can't walk either.

178
11:38.886 --> 11:41.514
I'm sorry. I was so insensitive back then.

179
11:41.597 --> 11:42.765
No, it's okay.

180
11:46.268 --> 11:47.269
Maybe next time…

181
11:49.522 --> 11:50.773
we could all get together.

182
11:52.566 --> 11:55.778
I feel bad that Hanako's stuck at home all the time.

183
11:55.861 --> 11:56.862
And somehow,

184
11:58.697 --> 12:00.115
you two have something in common.

185
12:02.117 --> 12:04.829
You should meet her sometime.

186
12:10.209 --> 12:11.544
I'm waiting for your answer,

187
12:12.670 --> 12:13.546
Ms. Lee Ga-kyung.

188
12:15.965 --> 12:16.799
Sure.

189
12:21.053 --> 12:23.848
I'm meeting him at Myeongwolgwan, right around the corner.

190
12:23.931 --> 12:26.141
I'm going to be late. See you tomorrow.

191
12:34.900 --> 12:36.360
He's gone.

192
12:42.199 --> 12:43.909
Will there be a next time?

193
12:47.997 --> 12:48.956
You're all set.

194
13:16.400 --> 13:17.234
So-ran.

195
13:21.780 --> 13:24.199
There's only one thing you need to think about.

196
13:25.701 --> 13:26.744
Your safety.

197
13:29.330 --> 13:30.998
No matter what happens tonight,

198
13:31.081 --> 13:33.667
you're coming back to this house safe and sound.

199
13:37.588 --> 13:38.422
Shall we go?

200
13:48.432 --> 13:52.603
The guests are coming over for dinner with Father.

201
13:52.686 --> 13:55.981
So why are you cleaning the study?

202
13:56.607 --> 13:59.944
Because the guests might want to look around the study.

203
14:00.027 --> 14:01.320
The study?

204
14:01.403 --> 14:03.322
What's there to see in the study?

205
14:03.822 --> 14:05.908
There's nothing but books.

206
14:06.617 --> 14:09.870
They might want to smoke in here.

207
14:09.954 --> 14:10.788
Smoke?

208
14:12.706 --> 14:16.961
Hideo can't handle being around so much cigarette smoke.

209
14:17.503 --> 14:19.755
So, who's coming over?

210
14:20.589 --> 14:23.676
Goodness, you're asking a lot of questions today.

211
14:23.759 --> 14:25.636
I have no idea either.

212
14:25.719 --> 14:28.389
Things are chaotic now. Why are we having guests over?

213
14:29.014 --> 14:30.808
And he told me at the last minute.

214
14:30.891 --> 14:33.018
I said, who's coming over?

215
14:33.102 --> 14:35.062
Your guess is as good as mine.

216
14:35.145 --> 14:36.063
What did you say?

217
14:36.146 --> 14:39.358
Speak in a language I can understand.

218
14:39.441 --> 14:41.276
Yanagi!

219
14:42.444 --> 14:43.821
Yanagi!

220
14:45.364 --> 14:46.740
Yanagi!

221
14:51.161 --> 14:54.123
Our comrades are putting their lives on the line again today.

222
14:55.499 --> 14:57.292
And here I am, going off to Hwawol

223
14:57.376 --> 15:00.004
to enjoy some Japanese food just because my dad insists.

224
15:01.880 --> 15:03.298
What a joke.

225
15:04.508 --> 15:05.718
I'm absolutely pathetic.

226
15:07.636 --> 15:10.597
Not every member of our group takes part in every operation.

227
15:10.681 --> 15:12.307
We need to consider our next move.

228
15:12.391 --> 15:13.600
Don't be so hard on yourself.

229
15:14.184 --> 15:15.477
Will I ever get the chance

230
15:16.437 --> 15:18.105
to hold a gun or a knife

231
15:18.188 --> 15:20.024
instead of a purse or a hand mirror?

232
15:21.483 --> 15:23.527
Guns and knives aren't the only weapons.

233
15:24.862 --> 15:26.238
What's supposed to be my weapon?

234
15:28.032 --> 15:30.325
That my father's the worst pro-Japanese traitor in Joseon?

235
15:38.876 --> 15:41.086
I hear she's leaving for Shanghai after this operation.

236
15:44.840 --> 15:45.883
Shanghai…

237
15:49.553 --> 15:50.596
I'm jealous.

238
16:03.525 --> 16:04.443
Myung-nam.

239
16:06.111 --> 16:09.281
You're supposed to be a quiet and demure young lady.

240
16:09.364 --> 16:10.824
Don't forget to act like one.

241
16:11.533 --> 16:13.160
What are you talking about?

242
16:13.243 --> 16:14.161
Aren't you getting in?

243
16:15.329 --> 16:18.207
Especially around your fiancé, keep your voice down

244
16:18.290 --> 16:19.750
and your temper in check.

245
16:19.833 --> 16:20.834
Do you understand?

246
16:20.918 --> 16:22.461
What? My fiancé?

247
16:23.087 --> 16:27.758
I must say, your future father-in-law has quite a sense of humor.

248
16:28.967 --> 16:31.804
Anyway, go there and make sure you smile a lot today.

249
16:31.887 --> 16:32.721
All right.

250
16:32.805 --> 16:34.348
Young-bok, get moving.

251
16:38.936 --> 16:39.978
What's going on?

252
16:40.062 --> 16:42.064
My father and the inspector general

253
16:42.147 --> 16:45.317
plotted to trick me into meeting Sato Hideo?

254
16:45.400 --> 16:46.235
Yes.

255
16:46.735 --> 16:47.569
That's great.

256
16:47.653 --> 16:49.154
What's great about that?

257
16:49.655 --> 16:50.989
No way. I'm not going.

258
16:53.742 --> 16:54.576
Hold on.

259
16:56.370 --> 16:58.580
So Sato Hideo won't be at his residence.

260
16:59.248 --> 17:00.582
He's coming to Hwawol instead?

261
17:03.919 --> 17:04.920
Let's take a gun with us.

262
17:15.180 --> 17:16.974
Welcome, Mr. Yoo.

263
17:18.225 --> 17:19.101
Mrs. Yoo.

264
17:20.144 --> 17:21.145
How have you been?

265
17:21.645 --> 17:23.689
Thanks for coming on such short notice.

266
17:24.815 --> 17:27.359
I've been meaning to have you two over to my residence.

267
17:28.110 --> 17:29.278
I'm sorry it took so long.

268
17:29.862 --> 17:32.447
Not at all. We're grateful for your kind invitation.

269
17:35.409 --> 17:37.703
This is my daughter, Hanako.

270
17:38.453 --> 17:39.288
Hanako.

271
17:56.513 --> 17:59.224
It's lovely to meet you, Miss Hanako.

272
18:00.434 --> 18:01.351
Hello.

273
18:02.477 --> 18:04.438
What a lovely young lady.

274
18:07.232 --> 18:08.066
Yanagi.

275
18:12.321 --> 18:14.948
We'll get you to your room now.

276
18:15.824 --> 18:19.077
We have company, so don't wander around.

277
18:22.998 --> 18:24.499
Please, right this way.

278
18:25.918 --> 18:27.836
Mr. Hideo doesn't seem to be here.

279
18:30.672 --> 18:33.634
Hideo had a prior engagement, so he couldn't make it today.

280
18:55.239 --> 18:56.615
This way, please.

281
19:07.751 --> 19:08.794
Inspector General.

282
19:11.463 --> 19:15.050
Even from the foyer, the residence is as beautiful as I'd heard.

283
19:15.133 --> 19:18.011
Would you mind showing us around the place before dinner?

284
19:20.097 --> 19:21.473
That's a great idea.

285
19:22.599 --> 19:23.517
But

286
19:23.600 --> 19:26.436
I've prepared a rather special drink for this occasion.

287
19:26.520 --> 19:27.729
Let's start with dinner.

288
19:28.313 --> 19:30.565
It's a real honor. In fact…

289
19:32.985 --> 19:36.697
though I'm just a humble reporter, I happen to be quite an avid reader.

290
19:36.780 --> 19:39.157
I heard you had quite a collection of books.

291
19:39.241 --> 19:43.245
I was so curious about your study that I could hardly sleep last night.

292
19:45.539 --> 19:46.873
Didn't I just tell you?

293
19:48.083 --> 19:49.084
Sorry?

294
19:49.584 --> 19:51.336
I said I had something prepared.

295
19:54.381 --> 19:55.465
Very well.

296
19:57.843 --> 20:00.971
I've been so looking forward to having dinner with you both.

297
20:01.054 --> 20:04.433
I'd hate to see the food get cold.

298
20:04.516 --> 20:07.894
So let's enjoy dinner first and look around the residence afterward.

299
20:19.031 --> 20:21.450
OUT OF ORDER

300
20:41.053 --> 20:41.887
You're all set.

301
20:42.554 --> 20:43.680
Thank you very much.

302
20:50.270 --> 20:51.146
Hey, yobo.

303
20:55.359 --> 20:58.862
Are you from Gyeongdo Noodle House? I've never seen you before.

304
20:59.613 --> 21:01.406
Our regular deliveryman

305
21:01.490 --> 21:03.784
was hit by a car and got hurt.

306
21:04.451 --> 21:07.371
Gyeongdo Noodle House? That's for Mr. Mitarai in the pneumatic tube room.

307
21:07.996 --> 21:08.830
Let him in.

308
21:09.706 --> 21:10.707
Thank you.

309
21:14.628 --> 21:18.340
LADIES' ROOM

310
21:18.423 --> 21:20.884
OUT OF ORDER

311
21:26.848 --> 21:30.477
I was wondering what kind of naengmyeon he kept ordering.

312
21:30.560 --> 21:31.728
Gyeongdo Noodle House?

313
21:32.521 --> 21:35.065
Why do these Japanese guys have such weird taste buds?

314
21:35.148 --> 21:37.401
Right? I'm not a fan of this place either.

315
21:38.193 --> 21:39.778
Who else likes Gyeongdo Noodle House?

316
21:39.861 --> 21:40.904
There's someone.

317
21:41.655 --> 21:43.532
A Japanese guy with bad taste in food.

318
21:44.866 --> 21:49.204
He was always going on and on about Gyeongdo Noodle House's naengmyeon.

319
21:49.746 --> 21:53.250
He even told me to get a job there so he could get a discount.

320
21:54.126 --> 21:55.210
Unbelievable.

321
21:56.002 --> 21:58.004
When it comes to naengmyeon, nothing beats

322
21:58.088 --> 21:59.714
-Hanseong Cold… -Hanseong Cold Noodles.

323
22:04.094 --> 22:05.178
Finally, someone with good taste.

324
22:19.818 --> 22:22.070
I hope you enjoy the food.

325
22:23.155 --> 22:24.114
You're too kind.

326
22:24.614 --> 22:27.701
People like us don't get to visit a place like this every day.

327
22:28.368 --> 22:30.829
Truth be told, I don't host dinners very often.

328
22:30.912 --> 22:33.832
My wife was the one who normally arranged these gatherings.

329
22:35.250 --> 22:36.960
I heard your wife passed away last year.

330
22:37.043 --> 22:38.336
Accept my belated condolences.

331
22:38.420 --> 22:39.337
I appreciate that.

332
22:39.963 --> 22:41.590
She was frail for most of her life.

333
22:43.300 --> 22:44.801
Hanako's from my previous marriage.

334
22:46.178 --> 22:49.389
I had a Joseon wife, but she died in childbirth.

335
22:51.641 --> 22:53.268
Anyway, Mr. Yoo.

336
22:53.768 --> 22:55.729
How are things going for you in Joseon?

337
22:55.812 --> 22:58.398
I hear you've been traveling all over Joseon for your reporting.

338
22:59.191 --> 23:01.485
I've been staying in Gyeongseong for the most part lately.

339
23:02.736 --> 23:03.612
I see.

340
23:05.322 --> 23:08.783
Back when I was a soldier, I traveled all over Joseon myself.

341
23:09.618 --> 23:10.577
Hamgyong-do,

342
23:11.161 --> 23:13.497
Gangwon-do, Jeolla-do, and Gyeongsang-do.

343
23:13.997 --> 23:17.000
It was fun trying the specialties of each region.

344
23:17.584 --> 23:22.422
Seeing all these local specialties from Joseon in one place makes me feel…

345
23:27.761 --> 23:29.679
What's that word in the Joseon language again?

346
23:31.431 --> 23:32.599
Nostalgic.

347
23:34.434 --> 23:36.102
It makes me feel nostalgic.

348
23:40.357 --> 23:42.150
These bamboo shoots are from Jeolla-do.

349
23:42.234 --> 23:43.360
They're in season right now.

350
23:43.443 --> 23:44.945
Do you like bamboo shoots, Mrs. Yoo?

351
23:46.112 --> 23:46.947
Yes.

352
23:47.030 --> 23:49.407
I heard bamboo shoots are common in Chinese cuisine.

353
23:50.283 --> 23:51.660
Where is your hometown?

354
23:52.661 --> 23:53.745
I'm from Shanghai.

355
23:54.371 --> 23:55.247
Shanghai.

356
23:55.330 --> 23:56.540
It's a fine city.

357
23:57.499 --> 24:01.503
You're probably still not very familiar with Joseon cuisine, are you?

358
24:02.128 --> 24:04.714
She's not used to Joseon food yet.

359
24:04.798 --> 24:06.091
I can imagine.

360
24:06.174 --> 24:08.802
Then this should be quite an experience for you.

361
24:09.511 --> 24:11.638
Joseon has plenty of interesting dishes.

362
24:15.225 --> 24:16.309
I'll give you an example.

363
24:17.310 --> 24:19.479
Do you know a dish called chutang tofu soup?

364
24:22.983 --> 24:24.025
It's also called chutang,

365
24:24.526 --> 24:26.236
or chueo tofu.

366
24:27.737 --> 24:29.739
It's a dish made by boiling loaches.

367
24:30.949 --> 24:33.535
The fascinating thing about this dish is how it's made.

368
24:34.661 --> 24:36.913
First, you put the loaches in cold water

369
24:36.997 --> 24:40.208
with the tofu, then slowly turn up the heat.

370
24:42.752 --> 24:44.963
Do you know what the loaches do when the water gets hot?

371
24:48.967 --> 24:52.804
To avoid the boiling water, they wriggle their way into the tofu.

372
24:54.598 --> 24:57.142
They believe they can hold out inside the tofu.

373
24:57.225 --> 25:01.438
But once the water boils, the tofu heats up too, doesn't it?

374
25:01.980 --> 25:05.650
So the loaches end up being cooked inside the tofu.

375
25:07.235 --> 25:08.403
I have

376
25:08.486 --> 25:10.989
never quite understood those loaches.

377
25:12.699 --> 25:14.284
The water is boiling,

378
25:15.243 --> 25:18.538
so how could they think they'd survive by hiding inside the tofu?

379
25:19.998 --> 25:21.499
Do you get it, Mrs. Yoo?

380
25:25.295 --> 25:27.005
Well, it does make for a delicacy.

381
25:27.088 --> 25:30.216
I suppose we don't really need to know what the loaches think.

382
25:34.012 --> 25:35.430
This rice cake

383
25:35.972 --> 25:38.350
is made with rice from a village in Gyeonggi-do.

384
25:38.850 --> 25:40.977
The place was famous for its fertile land.

385
25:42.395 --> 25:44.648
I believe it was called Kyeam-ri.

386
25:59.204 --> 26:01.539
It was a place with vast stretches of farmland.

387
26:03.083 --> 26:06.002
There was a bit of trouble there a long time ago.

388
26:10.715 --> 26:13.385
I see. What about the wild spring greens--

389
26:13.468 --> 26:15.220
There was a man in that village.

390
26:16.388 --> 26:17.389
That man

391
26:17.889 --> 26:20.517
never revealed his comrades' names, even until the very end.

392
26:21.101 --> 26:22.435
He wouldn't talk

393
26:23.853 --> 26:25.980
even when we pointed a gun at his daughter

394
26:26.815 --> 26:28.191
right in front of him.

395
26:34.531 --> 26:35.657
Shoot.

396
26:35.740 --> 26:36.908
No!

397
26:42.080 --> 26:45.542
He chose his convictions over his own child.

398
26:46.167 --> 26:48.294
I have to admit, I was quite impressed.

399
26:58.513 --> 27:00.056
I almost forgot the wine.

400
27:00.724 --> 27:01.975
This one's from 1919.

401
27:02.642 --> 27:03.852
Thirteen years.

402
27:03.935 --> 27:05.311
It's aged quite a bit.

403
27:06.855 --> 27:08.440
A fine wine is best

404
27:09.357 --> 27:11.568
when you've let it age.

405
27:13.820 --> 27:14.779
But

406
27:14.863 --> 27:16.698
what happened next is even more interesting.

407
27:19.242 --> 27:23.121
Only after his daughter died did he finally give up his comrades' names.

408
27:23.955 --> 27:25.498
Of course, it was too late.

409
27:26.791 --> 27:27.959
Why would he do that?

410
27:28.501 --> 27:31.296
He kept his mouth shut while his daughter was alive,

411
27:31.379 --> 27:33.047
but finally spoke after she died.

412
27:34.090 --> 27:36.426
He's like those loaches, wouldn't you say?

413
27:42.557 --> 27:44.434
He thought he could protect his daughter

414
27:44.976 --> 27:47.353
if he held out and stayed true to his beliefs.

415
27:47.437 --> 27:48.605
But in the end,

416
27:49.481 --> 27:52.817
he failed to protect his daughter or stay true to his beliefs.

417
27:54.486 --> 27:56.321
It's all so pointless, isn't it?

418
28:12.253 --> 28:14.798
So the carrier should reach Sato's study

419
28:14.881 --> 28:17.175
sometime between 6:30 p.m. and 6:40 p.m.

420
28:17.258 --> 28:18.134
Right.

421
28:19.636 --> 28:22.847
I'll stall him and make sure he's in the study until then.

422
28:24.224 --> 28:25.600
His wife

423
28:25.683 --> 28:27.560
was there too.

424
28:29.103 --> 28:30.021
Mrs. Yoo.

425
28:30.855 --> 28:33.066
How do you think that woman went on living after that?

426
28:35.360 --> 28:37.445
Sir, you have a phone call.

427
28:37.529 --> 28:38.947
There are two possibilities.

428
28:39.531 --> 28:40.490
She either

429
28:40.573 --> 28:42.826
kept her daughter in her heart and lived quietly,

430
28:43.743 --> 28:44.577
or…

431
28:46.329 --> 28:47.956
lived for the day she could get revenge.

432
28:56.714 --> 28:59.384
If she decided to get revenge,

433
28:59.467 --> 29:00.301
well,

434
29:01.469 --> 29:02.720
what do you think would happen?

435
29:03.471 --> 29:04.597
Inspector General.

436
29:11.104 --> 29:12.981
It's an old Chinese proverb.

437
29:14.274 --> 29:15.358
In the Joseon language,

438
29:16.359 --> 29:19.529
cheonmanghoehoe, soibullu.

439
29:19.612 --> 29:21.489
THOSE WHO DO WRONG CAN'T ESCAPE HEAVEN'S WRATH

440
29:25.535 --> 29:28.413
Heaven's net may look wide and full of holes,

441
29:29.664 --> 29:31.791
yet it lets nothing through.

442
29:36.421 --> 29:38.464
I see your Joseon language has improved quite a bit.

443
29:38.548 --> 29:39.424
Yes.

444
29:40.842 --> 29:42.677
It's a very wise saying.

445
29:42.760 --> 29:44.137
It certainly is.

446
29:45.388 --> 29:46.389
In other words,

447
29:47.640 --> 29:49.726
justice will prevail,

448
29:49.809 --> 29:52.937
so there's no need to take matters into our own hands, is there?

449
29:53.938 --> 29:55.940
If you forget your place and get involved,

450
29:56.441 --> 30:00.111
you may end up getting caught in Heaven's net.

451
30:05.033 --> 30:05.867
Come in.

452
30:09.662 --> 30:10.705
I'm sorry to interrupt.

453
30:10.788 --> 30:12.081
What is it?

454
30:12.165 --> 30:14.918
A pneumatic tube carrier has arrived from the Government-General.

455
30:15.001 --> 30:16.377
Leave it there.

456
30:16.461 --> 30:17.754
Yes, sir.

457
30:27.513 --> 30:28.848
Would you mind opening it for me?

458
30:31.017 --> 30:32.727
I can't get this wine open.

459
30:40.485 --> 30:44.155
I'd hate to break it by opening it myself.

460
30:44.238 --> 30:45.823
Allow me to open the wine bottle.

461
30:46.449 --> 30:47.492
Very well, then.

462
31:02.924 --> 31:04.050
Can't you get it open?

463
31:05.802 --> 31:06.636
No, it's fine.

464
31:39.210 --> 31:40.044
There we go.

465
32:13.244 --> 32:14.912
I have one more little surprise

466
32:16.164 --> 32:17.874
for both of you.

467
32:22.879 --> 32:23.880
I think Keum Seo-hee

468
32:25.048 --> 32:26.132
is a spy.

469
32:30.219 --> 32:32.597
This means Keum Seo-hee

470
32:33.181 --> 32:34.015
is under arrest.

471
32:34.098 --> 32:34.932
COMPLETE

472
32:40.354 --> 32:42.148
There was a man named Keum Seok-jung.

473
32:43.107 --> 32:46.194
It was the foolish father from Kyeam-ri that I just mentioned.

474
32:47.361 --> 32:49.781
He got caught recently after trying to kill me.

475
32:51.699 --> 32:53.451
As it happens, his daughter's name

476
32:54.702 --> 32:55.995
was Keum Seo-hee.

477
32:57.413 --> 33:00.917
Do you want us to arrest Keum Seo-hee tonight?

478
33:01.834 --> 33:03.002
But we don't have proof--

479
33:03.086 --> 33:05.129
The name Keum Seo-hee

480
33:05.797 --> 33:06.631
is proof.

481
33:08.132 --> 33:09.342
Keum Seo-hee.

482
33:11.094 --> 33:14.097
Keum Seok-jung's wife named her after the daughter she'd lost.

483
33:15.389 --> 33:17.642
That means they have a special bond.

484
33:18.976 --> 33:21.145
If a woman who'd already lost a child

485
33:22.063 --> 33:24.982
found another girl with the same name in danger,

486
33:26.150 --> 33:28.111
could she possibly stay calm?

487
33:39.080 --> 33:41.374
When Interpreter Trainee Keum Seo-hee leaves for the day,

488
33:41.457 --> 33:43.042
don't let her leave the building.

489
33:43.126 --> 33:43.960
Yes, sir.

490
34:15.283 --> 34:16.367
Hello.

491
34:16.450 --> 34:17.910
RECORDS ROOM

492
34:27.837 --> 34:28.796
How may I help you?

493
34:50.359 --> 34:53.779
Keum Seo-hee must be closely connected to Keum Seok-jung and his circle.

494
34:53.863 --> 34:56.782
That's why I had Keum Seo-hee arrested

495
34:56.866 --> 34:59.243
and brought directly here.

496
35:01.037 --> 35:03.789
We'll find out once we question her.

497
35:04.457 --> 35:05.791
She should be on her way here.

498
35:06.792 --> 35:07.960
She was your live-in maid.

499
35:08.586 --> 35:10.254
I guess she deceived you both.

500
35:10.338 --> 35:12.215
Wouldn't it be best to confront her in person?

501
35:18.638 --> 35:20.431
MYEONGWOLGWAN

502
35:24.769 --> 35:26.437
Once we hear from the inspector general,

503
35:26.520 --> 35:28.356
-arrest him right away. -Yes, sir.

504
35:30.900 --> 35:33.986
HWAWOL

505
35:52.505 --> 35:53.756
In hindsight,

506
35:53.839 --> 35:56.926
there were plenty of suspicious things about her from day one.

507
35:57.593 --> 36:01.597
Most Joseon people would lower their heads just passing the Government-General.

508
36:02.515 --> 36:04.684
Yet she had the nerve to work there

509
36:05.476 --> 36:08.354
and come and go as if she owned the place.

510
36:09.063 --> 36:11.607
And she certainly knew how to do her job.

511
36:11.691 --> 36:13.067
You saw her at the banquet.

512
36:14.652 --> 36:17.822
I bet she was sharp when she served you as your maid.

513
36:18.531 --> 36:19.448
What was she like?

514
36:24.745 --> 36:27.498
I'm afraid there's been a misunderstanding.

515
36:27.999 --> 36:28.916
Seo-hee is just--

516
36:29.000 --> 36:31.711
She had the nerve to join the Government-General as a spy.

517
36:31.794 --> 36:33.462
She's quite a bold little thing.

518
36:34.672 --> 36:36.632
I have to admire her nerve.

519
36:36.716 --> 36:40.177
It's a shame she threw her life away for such a foolish cause.

520
36:45.766 --> 36:47.643
Once we take her into custody,

521
36:47.727 --> 36:51.147
we'll have to search your home, so I hope you'll understand.

522
36:51.731 --> 36:53.441
There's no need to be concerned.

523
36:53.524 --> 36:55.985
Neither of you is involved in this matter, are you?

524
37:02.616 --> 37:03.534
Or am I wrong?

525
37:05.119 --> 37:06.412
Are you involved?

526
37:11.000 --> 37:13.169
The chief of police is here, sir.

527
37:23.220 --> 37:24.055
Let him in.

528
37:32.104 --> 37:33.022
Inspector General.

529
37:55.378 --> 37:56.253
How could this be?

530
38:22.863 --> 38:24.740
20 MINUTES AGO

531
38:24.824 --> 38:26.826
ENGLISH TRANSLATION UNIT

532
38:33.332 --> 38:34.542
So she's still here?

533
38:34.625 --> 38:35.626
Yes.

534
38:35.709 --> 38:37.545
She should be in the Foreign Affairs Division.

535
38:37.628 --> 38:39.338
Why are we supposed to arrest her?

536
38:39.839 --> 38:41.382
I'm not really sure.

537
39:07.199 --> 39:08.909
There you are. Let's hurry.

538
39:08.993 --> 39:10.202
Okay.

539
39:12.371 --> 39:14.790
Your naengmyeon is here.

540
39:14.874 --> 39:15.916
Come in.

541
39:16.000 --> 39:16.834
Yes, sir!

542
39:24.425 --> 39:26.093
The bombs. I need to get the bombs out.

543
39:31.182 --> 39:32.683
Hello there.

544
39:32.766 --> 39:33.642
Ms. Keum.

545
39:47.198 --> 39:48.616
That looked perfect.

546
39:48.699 --> 39:50.034
Why are you wiping it off?

547
39:50.117 --> 39:51.535
I don't like it.

548
40:08.886 --> 40:10.387
It looks perfect now!

549
40:10.471 --> 40:12.598
-It really does! -No.

550
40:13.098 --> 40:15.809
Wearing lipstick is all about the heart.

551
40:16.393 --> 40:19.104
If your heart isn't right,

552
40:19.897 --> 40:22.191
then your lips are a lie.

553
40:23.901 --> 40:24.985
Is that so?

554
40:38.040 --> 40:39.083
Hey, you.

555
40:39.166 --> 40:40.626
I've never seen you before.

556
40:41.168 --> 40:42.336
Are you the new yobo?

557
40:43.045 --> 40:43.879
Sorry?

558
40:43.963 --> 40:44.797
"Sorry?"

559
40:46.465 --> 40:47.925
You ignorant fool.

560
40:48.008 --> 40:50.219
You can't even understand basic Japanese.

561
40:50.886 --> 40:53.055
You Josenjings are hopeless.

562
40:53.138 --> 40:56.809
No matter how much we Japanese teach you, you're still useless.

563
40:56.892 --> 40:58.394
You imbecile.

564
40:58.477 --> 40:59.395
Do you understand?

565
41:06.068 --> 41:09.446
You don't even know what I'm saying. You just stand there smiling.

566
41:09.530 --> 41:10.781
What a pathetic moron.

567
41:11.448 --> 41:12.449
Get out of here!

568
41:12.950 --> 41:14.285
Come back when I call you.

569
41:15.286 --> 41:16.120
Yes, sir.

570
41:16.870 --> 41:18.330
What a complete moron.

571
41:20.791 --> 41:21.750
This is so good!

572
41:25.045 --> 41:26.171
Mr. Sato.

573
41:26.255 --> 41:27.840
What brings you back?

574
41:28.716 --> 41:30.759
I'd like to call someone from the staff.

575
41:31.719 --> 41:33.262
Could you pass this along for me?

576
41:33.345 --> 41:35.306
I'm running late for dinner.

577
41:35.389 --> 41:36.765
Sure, I'll take it.

578
41:38.434 --> 41:40.102
Who should I deliver it to?

579
41:41.395 --> 41:43.480
No, actually, I'll deliver it myself.

580
41:43.564 --> 41:44.398
Yes, sir.

581
41:46.567 --> 41:48.193
Keum Seo-hee isn't in there!

582
41:48.277 --> 41:49.737
Maybe she caught on and ran away.

583
41:49.820 --> 41:50.821
Find her! Now!

584
41:50.904 --> 41:51.822
Yes, sir!

585
41:51.905 --> 41:54.199
We've made sure she can't leave the building.

586
42:05.085 --> 42:06.086
Oh, look.

587
42:06.795 --> 42:08.547
We're wearing similar outfits.

588
42:09.340 --> 42:12.885
Mine is from Ginza Boutique.

589
42:12.968 --> 42:14.428
Where did you get yours?

590
42:16.347 --> 42:18.515
That's not important right now.

591
42:23.020 --> 42:24.647
Yes, you're right!

592
42:25.230 --> 42:27.149
Clothes are important.

593
42:27.232 --> 42:28.567
Where did you get yours?

594
42:28.651 --> 42:31.153
You didn't have it made in Jongno, did you?

595
42:31.236 --> 42:34.865
Clothes made by Josenjings look a little cheap to me.

596
42:34.948 --> 42:36.533
Oh, no offense.

597
42:37.660 --> 42:38.494
No, it's fine.

598
42:41.955 --> 42:43.749
Listen, Ms. Yamada.

599
42:45.668 --> 42:48.796
You know, about Interpreter Sato.

600
42:49.421 --> 42:51.715
Yes? What about him?

601
42:52.675 --> 42:54.259
About his engagement…

602
42:54.802 --> 42:55.928
The truth is…

603
42:57.429 --> 42:59.473
it's an arranged marriage without love.

604
43:02.810 --> 43:03.727
Because…

605
43:05.771 --> 43:08.065
deep in his heart,

606
43:08.899 --> 43:09.775
he's always loved

607
43:10.442 --> 43:11.360
you, Ms. Yamada.

608
43:12.736 --> 43:13.570
Oh my.

609
43:15.531 --> 43:16.365
Actually,

610
43:16.990 --> 43:19.827
Mr. Sato is in the Records Room at the moment.

611
43:19.910 --> 43:20.869
Records Room?

612
43:20.953 --> 43:23.372
Yes, because of work.

613
43:23.455 --> 43:24.915
He's there alone.

614
43:26.041 --> 43:26.917
What if

615
43:27.000 --> 43:30.212
you went to the Records Room right now?

616
43:30.796 --> 43:31.880
You might,

617
43:31.964 --> 43:33.382
by pure coincidence…

618
43:33.465 --> 43:35.426
-Run into each other. -Yes, exactly!

619
43:35.509 --> 43:36.593
Do you see what I mean?

620
43:36.677 --> 43:40.472
Romance in popular fiction always starts in a library.

621
43:40.556 --> 43:44.017
Imagine you and Mr. Sato alone in the Records Room.

622
43:44.101 --> 43:46.854
Then a pile of books comes tumbling off the shelves.

623
43:48.731 --> 43:50.107
My goodness!

624
43:50.190 --> 43:52.860
That's all I'll say!

625
43:52.943 --> 43:54.695
What do I do?

626
43:54.778 --> 43:56.196
Go on, hurry!

627
43:57.656 --> 43:59.116
Wait, what do I do?

628
43:59.700 --> 44:00.617
It's flawless!

629
44:00.701 --> 44:01.910
Come on, off you go.

630
44:01.994 --> 44:02.953
Do my lips look okay?

631
44:03.036 --> 44:04.747
They look fine. Now go see him.

632
44:14.548 --> 44:18.093
OUT OF ORDER

633
44:25.058 --> 44:28.979
When the time comes, go in first and send it.

634
44:29.855 --> 44:31.315
I need to take care of something.

635
44:32.191 --> 44:33.275
Okay.

636
44:39.865 --> 44:41.033
Hello.

637
44:42.826 --> 44:43.952
YAMADA HANAKO

638
44:45.370 --> 44:47.456
I'm here to find some records.

639
44:47.539 --> 44:48.791
Of course.

640
44:48.874 --> 44:50.709
KEUM SEO-HEE

641
45:16.819 --> 45:17.945
When the books

642
45:18.654 --> 45:21.615
come tumbling down…

643
45:22.324 --> 45:23.158
Mr. Sato

644
45:24.159 --> 45:26.161
would protect me like this, wouldn't he?

645
45:27.120 --> 45:28.288
And then…

646
45:32.793 --> 45:34.086
What do I do?

647
45:36.296 --> 45:39.800
It's embarrassing with the lights this bright.

648
45:46.014 --> 45:47.933
Come on, please come this way.

649
46:02.281 --> 46:03.490
Can I help you?

650
46:17.337 --> 46:18.297
Mr. Hideo?

651
46:35.856 --> 46:37.274
I'm so sorry.

652
46:53.874 --> 46:55.792
Send this to the inspector general's residence.

653
46:55.876 --> 46:56.793
Yes, sir.

654
47:05.427 --> 47:08.847
Operator, put me through to the inspector general's residence.

655
47:14.728 --> 47:15.562
Hello?

656
47:15.646 --> 47:18.440
This is the Government-General's pneumatic tube room.

657
47:18.523 --> 47:21.026
We're sending a pneumatic tube carrier to the residence.

658
47:21.109 --> 47:22.402
Understood.

659
47:33.330 --> 47:34.498
INSPECTOR GENERAL

660
47:51.598 --> 47:52.516
Se-hwan.

661
47:53.642 --> 47:55.352
Please make it out in one piece.

662
48:02.234 --> 48:03.360
That delivery boy went in a while ago.

663
48:03.860 --> 48:05.946
What's taking him so long?

664
48:11.952 --> 48:13.704
Yobo! Come collect the bowl!

665
48:23.130 --> 48:25.257
Why are you so slow?

666
48:25.340 --> 48:26.758
Get the bowl out of here!

667
48:26.842 --> 48:29.720
Josenjings are always so slow.

668
49:04.421 --> 49:05.338
It's me.

669
49:20.020 --> 49:21.271
-Hello, Mr. Sato. -Hello.

670
49:22.439 --> 49:24.483
-Excuse me. -Yes?

671
49:24.566 --> 49:26.735
You're the guard posted at the side gate, aren't you?

672
49:27.360 --> 49:28.487
Is something going on?

673
49:28.570 --> 49:29.988
You were looking for someone.

674
49:30.989 --> 49:33.575
The naengmyeon delivery boy went to the pneumatic tube room

675
49:33.658 --> 49:35.452
and hasn't come out, so I'm looking for him.

676
49:36.161 --> 49:38.288
I wanted to make sure everything was okay.

677
49:38.371 --> 49:40.665
Then I'll go see what's going on.

678
49:40.749 --> 49:42.250
You shouldn't leave your post.

679
49:42.334 --> 49:44.211
-But-- -It's all right.

680
49:44.294 --> 49:48.090
I just remembered I needed to go to the pneumatic tube room anyway.

681
49:48.173 --> 49:49.549
I'll check on him while I'm there.

682
49:49.633 --> 49:51.134
Thank you very much, Mr. Sato.

683
49:59.518 --> 50:01.686
Never let Keum Seo-hee leave the building.

684
50:01.770 --> 50:03.313
Search every inch of the building!

685
50:03.396 --> 50:05.941
We have to find her before the chief of police gets here!

686
50:06.024 --> 50:07.025
-Yes, sir! -Yes, sir!

687
50:08.777 --> 50:10.403
Just wait until I catch you.

688
50:10.987 --> 50:12.864
You sneaky little rat.

689
50:20.914 --> 50:21.957
What's taking him so long?

690
50:22.958 --> 50:25.043
He doesn't seem like the type to be late.

691
50:27.712 --> 50:28.713
Something feels off.

692
50:34.344 --> 50:35.762
Take me to the Government-General.

693
50:35.846 --> 50:37.514
Something must be going on there.

694
50:47.190 --> 50:48.233
We're all set.

695
50:53.864 --> 50:56.199
Please connect me to the governor-general's residence.

696
51:03.498 --> 51:04.749
Hello?

697
51:04.833 --> 51:05.792
Hello?

698
51:05.876 --> 51:08.128
This is the Government-General's pneumatic tube room.

699
51:08.211 --> 51:10.714
We're sending a pneumatic tube carrier to the governor-general.

700
51:10.797 --> 51:12.299
Make sure he receives it now.

701
51:14.968 --> 51:15.802
Sorry?

702
51:15.886 --> 51:17.971
It can't be delivered to His Excellency

703
51:18.054 --> 51:19.598
for another hour or so.

704
51:19.681 --> 51:21.683
He's taking a bath right now.

705
51:21.766 --> 51:23.602
He's taking a bath?

706
51:24.895 --> 51:26.354
Okay, understood.

707
51:28.607 --> 51:29.441
What do we do?

708
51:29.524 --> 51:32.360
Let's send it to the inspector general's residence first.

709
51:35.697 --> 51:38.283
Operator, please put me through to the inspector general's residence.

710
51:54.758 --> 51:55.842
No one's answering.

711
51:57.636 --> 51:59.304
No one's answering at the residence.

712
52:03.141 --> 52:05.143
Could you try one more time?

713
52:07.771 --> 52:08.855
Mr. Mitarai.

714
52:12.275 --> 52:13.443
Mr. Mitarai.

715
52:15.153 --> 52:16.154
Are you there?

716
52:23.286 --> 52:24.579
Ms. Keum. It's me.

717
52:26.081 --> 52:27.249
You're in there, aren't you?

718
52:28.333 --> 52:29.417
Come out right now.

719
52:29.501 --> 52:32.754
The police are looking everywhere to arrest you.

720
52:32.837 --> 52:34.464
You have to run now.

721
52:35.131 --> 52:36.508
Is that Sato Hideo outside?

722
52:37.968 --> 52:39.719
Surely you're not falling for that?

723
52:41.179 --> 52:43.014
He's trying to arrest us.

724
52:47.394 --> 52:48.853
Let's send it anyway.

725
52:48.937 --> 52:50.021
What?

726
52:51.064 --> 52:52.440
INSPECTOR GENERAL

727
52:57.696 --> 52:59.197
I know you're in there.

728
53:00.490 --> 53:01.908
Please open the door.

729
53:01.992 --> 53:03.618
You have to trust me.

730
53:04.411 --> 53:05.245
Lee Ga-kyung!

731
53:07.914 --> 53:09.207
Get a hold of yourself.

732
53:14.045 --> 53:16.089
Put me through to the inspector general's residence.

733
53:16.923 --> 53:18.174
I'm sorry, sir!

734
53:18.258 --> 53:20.135
There must have been some mistake!

735
53:20.218 --> 53:21.845
I'll go get her myself immediately!

736
53:34.149 --> 53:35.150
Yanagi.

737
53:38.361 --> 53:39.321
Yanagi!

738
53:50.832 --> 53:51.666
Hello?

739
53:52.292 --> 53:53.460
Hello?

740
53:56.212 --> 53:57.047
What's wrong?

741
53:58.548 --> 53:59.924
A little girl answered.

742
54:00.842 --> 54:02.052
I think she's Sato's daughter.

743
54:02.761 --> 54:03.595
What?

744
54:04.888 --> 54:07.390
I've got a little sister. Her name is Hanako.

745
54:08.641 --> 54:09.642
Hello?

746
54:11.227 --> 54:12.479
Hello?

747
54:12.562 --> 54:13.563
Is this Hanako?

748
54:13.646 --> 54:14.814
What?

749
54:14.898 --> 54:17.192
How do you know my name?

750
54:17.275 --> 54:20.612
I'm a friend of your brother Hideo's.

751
54:20.695 --> 54:23.490
Hanako, are you in the study right now?

752
54:24.240 --> 54:26.242
Yes. Why?

753
54:27.243 --> 54:29.746
Could you put your father on the phone?

754
54:29.829 --> 54:31.247
I have an urgent matter to discuss.

755
54:31.831 --> 54:33.124
I can't.

756
54:33.208 --> 54:36.586
He's having dinner with guests right now.

757
54:36.669 --> 54:38.421
Okay, Hanako.

758
54:38.922 --> 54:41.466
Please get out of there right now.

759
54:42.050 --> 54:44.511
Wait, who are you?

760
54:45.136 --> 54:46.179
Are you…

761
54:47.180 --> 54:48.807
my brother's girlfriend?

762
54:49.474 --> 54:50.308
Well…

763
54:50.975 --> 54:51.851
Yes, I am.

764
54:51.935 --> 54:53.937
So come on, get out of there.

765
54:54.020 --> 54:54.854
You're lying.

766
54:54.938 --> 54:56.815
My brother doesn't have a girlfriend!

767
54:59.609 --> 55:00.443
Come on out.

768
55:01.528 --> 55:03.321
You need to run!

769
55:08.827 --> 55:09.661
Hanako.

770
55:11.329 --> 55:12.163
Wait.

771
55:12.247 --> 55:13.248
Something's arrived.

772
55:13.331 --> 55:16.126
Don't open that! Leave the room now!

773
55:16.209 --> 55:18.545
Why are you speaking to me informally?

774
55:19.796 --> 55:22.173
That thing is dangerous!

775
55:22.257 --> 55:24.259
Never, ever touch that.

776
55:24.342 --> 55:26.052
Get out of the study right now!

777
55:26.136 --> 55:27.804
Is it dangerous?

778
55:28.304 --> 55:29.222
How come?

779
55:29.305 --> 55:31.891
This came for my father.

780
55:32.851 --> 55:33.810
Please!

781
55:33.893 --> 55:36.312
You need to get out of there!

782
55:36.396 --> 55:38.273
Just leave it where it is!

783
55:42.360 --> 55:43.653
Here's white rice

784
55:44.320 --> 55:46.114
and chutang tofu soup.

785
55:52.662 --> 55:54.289
Who was that on the phone?

786
55:55.957 --> 55:57.375
Did someone call?

787
56:11.473 --> 56:12.807
Hanako!

788
56:12.891 --> 56:13.933
I'm begging you.

789
56:14.684 --> 56:16.728
Who are you, really?

790
56:16.811 --> 56:19.272
Are you really Hideo's girlfriend?

791
56:19.355 --> 56:22.650
No, that's not important right now. Just hurry…

792
56:24.486 --> 56:25.403
Lee Ga-kyung!

793
56:26.154 --> 56:27.238
What are you doing?

794
56:30.033 --> 56:30.992
Lee Ga-kyung!

795
56:32.619 --> 56:33.703
Mr. Sato.

796
56:34.621 --> 56:37.123
You're not Hideo's girlfriend, are you?

797
56:40.627 --> 56:41.628
Hello?

798
56:42.295 --> 56:43.296
Hello?

799
56:46.758 --> 56:47.592
Hanako.

800
56:52.764 --> 56:53.932
Hanako!

801
56:59.604 --> 57:00.480
Hanako.

802
57:02.357 --> 57:03.316
Hideo?

803
57:03.399 --> 57:04.651
Hanako.

804
57:04.734 --> 57:06.236
Listen to me carefully.

805
57:06.319 --> 57:08.655
You have to get out of the study now. Okay?

806
57:08.738 --> 57:10.907
Okay, I will.

807
57:17.330 --> 57:18.998
By the way, Hideo.

808
57:19.082 --> 57:21.292
-That lady just now. -Hanako.

809
57:21.376 --> 57:23.378
-Is she really your girlfriend? -Hanako.

810
57:23.461 --> 57:24.629
-She isn't, right? -Get out!

811
57:24.712 --> 57:25.547
-Hanako! -Hanako.

812
57:25.630 --> 57:26.965
Hanako!

813
57:27.048 --> 57:28.174
Who are you?

814
57:28.258 --> 57:29.217
So-ran.

815
57:47.193 --> 57:48.111
Hanako.

816
57:56.327 --> 57:57.704
Hanako. Hanako?

817
57:59.789 --> 58:00.623
Hanako.

818
58:01.749 --> 58:02.792
Hello?

819
58:04.544 --> 58:05.753
Hana… Hanako?

820
58:09.007 --> 58:10.049
Hanako!

821
59:18.534 --> 59:22.455
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

822
59:24.415 --> 59:26.417
Philip!

823
59:28.169 --> 59:30.546
Will you keep your mouth shut like your husband did

824
59:30.630 --> 59:32.256
even if I shoot her dead?

825
59:34.676 --> 59:35.885
Go ask them

826
59:35.968 --> 59:38.262
about my dead Joseon wife.

827
59:38.805 --> 59:39.847
You have the same eyes.

828
59:40.431 --> 59:41.391
Hideo.

829
59:41.474 --> 59:43.643
What's making you so confused?

830
59:43.726 --> 59:44.811
Independence for Korea!

831
59:44.894 --> 59:46.229
Hideo!

832
59:56.531 --> 59:58.533
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
